---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Corrections" description="How UK Places checks a reported error against the primary source, where figures from other sources are corrected, and where changes are recorded.">
  <main class="shell static-page" id="main-content">
    <section class="static-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p><h1>How errors are corrected.</h1><p>A geography record is only useful if it is right. Errors are checked against the primary source and fixed in the record.</p></section>
    <div class="static-content">
      <section><h2>Geography</h2><p>Codes, names, authority types, counties and regions are checked against the official source for each: the Office for National Statistics for codes and names, and Schedule 1 to the Lieutenancies Act 1997 for ceremonial counties. A reported error is compared with that source before anything changes. Where the source does not settle a value, the field is left blank.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Figures from other sources</h2><p>Each dated figure on a record comes from the specialist source named beside it. An error in such a figure is corrected at that source, and the record here follows at its next refresh.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Where changes are recorded</h2><p>Material changes to UK Places are listed with their dates on the <a href="/updates/">updates page</a>. Each record also shows the date it was last reviewed.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Reporting an error</h2><p>See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
